/-!
# Standard ↔ Eddington–Finkelstein: the actual coordinate map on the overlap

On the overlap `domStd M` (`r > 0`, `r ≠ 2M`, `0 < θ < π`; both the exterior and, for `M > 0`, the
interior component) we prove, for `ε = ±1`:

* `toEF M ε` and `fromEF M ε` are `C^∞` on `domStd M`, map `domStd M` into itself (⊆ `domEF`) and
  are mutually inverse (globally on the overlap, hence a diffeomorphism of `domStd M` onto itself);
* the Jacobian of `toEF` is the explicit matrix `jac`, its entries are the genuine partial
  derivatives (`HasDerivAt`, not junk values), and `det jac = 1`;
* pull-back identity: `gStd = jacᵀ · (gEF ∘ toEF) · jac` componentwise.

